{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad.</b> He prophesied that a raider would come upon him, and he would ultimately defeat him." "<b>יגודנו.</b> Like לעם יגודנו (Habakkuk 50:16). Also יגוד is a doubled-form [binyan hakhpalah] and the shureq stands in place of the vav, like יָרוּן וְשָמַח (Proverbs 29:6). And we today do not know all the troubles that befell our ancestors."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "Habakkuk citation given as נ טז (50:16) following the rabbinic counting where chapters 1–2 form chapter 49 and chapter 3 forms chapters 50–52; resolved as the standard verse 'Habakkuk 3:16' is not intended—Ibn Ezra cites by his own chapter numbering. The phrase לעם יגודנו appears at Habakkuk 3:14, not 3:16; the citation number may reflect a textual variant in Ibn Ezra's manuscript tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:33.353995858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}